WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.750
Every certificate I've ever been handed asked me to trust somebody.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.250
This one doesn't.

3
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:09.569
Here's what actually happens the moment you issue a

4
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:10.453
certificate.

5
00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:14.112
It's signed, and its fingerprint is sealed to the

6
00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:14.641
moment.

7
00:00:14.991 --> 00:00:19.757
That fingerprint goes out to the OpenTimestamps network, witnessed

8
00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:21.891
by two independent calendars.

9
00:00:22.241 --> 00:00:25.523
Within the hour, the next Bitcoin block folds it

10
00:00:25.523 --> 00:00:28.001
in, and the proof becomes permanent.

11
00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:33.135
You can check it yourself, right there. Not our

12
00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:34.431
word for it.

